- If <action> is RETRIEVE: one passage is appended (discounting your reward by factor r), then TURN 2 follows.
- <estimated_confidence> is scored against your actual TURN-2 confidence.

TURN 2 (only after RETRIEVE; a passage is provided; you MUST answer now) — output exactly:
<think> reason using the retrieved context </think>
<answer> your final short factual answer </answer>
<analysis> brief reasoning about whether it is correct </analysis>
<confidence> a single number in [0,1]: the probability this answer is correct </confidence>

Reward = correctness * (r ^ number_of_RETRIEVE), plus a calibration bonus when each <confidence> matches
your actual correctness, plus a bonus when <estimated_confidence> matches your turn-2 <confidence>.
Answer directly when confident; RETRIEVE only when it is likely to fix a wrong answer.
